\pard\sa160\b\fs28 Independent Claims\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa160\b\fs24 Claim 1\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa120 A computer-implemented method for authorizing a software agent to act on behalf of a principal, the method comprising:\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa120 receiving a task request associated with the principal;\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa120 identifying the software agent designated to perform at least a portion of the task request;\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa120 determining authorization constraints based on the task request, an identity of the principal, an identity of the software agent, and one or more policies;\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa120 generating a scoped authorization artifact encoding a bounded permission set for the software agent;\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa120 intercepting an action request generated by the software agent prior to execution of the action request;\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa120 validating the action request against the scoped authorization artifact using a compound authorization decision that includes at least a principal decision, an agent decision, and a delegation decision; and\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa120 selectively permitting, denying, modifying, or escalating execution of the action request based on the validating.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa160\b\fs24 Claim 2\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa120 The method of claim 1, wherein the compound authorization decision permits execution only when the principal decision, the agent decision, and the delegation decision each resolve to allow.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa160\b\fs24 Claim 3\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa120 The method of claim 1, wherein the scoped authorization artifact is bound to at least one of a task identifier, a tenant identifier, a permitted tool set, a permitted action set, a resource scope, a time window, an invocation limit, a spending threshold, a data sensitivity class, or a maximum delegation depth.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa160\b\fs24 Claim 4\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa120 The method of claim 1, wherein generating the scoped authorization artifact comprises cryptographically signing the scoped authorization artifact.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa160\b\fs24 Claim 5\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa120 The method of claim 1, wherein the scoped authorization artifact includes at least a delegation identifier and a root delegation identifier.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa160\b\fs24 Claim 6\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa120 The method of claim 1, wherein the authorization constraints include one or more classification caps associated with one or more classification hierarchies.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa160\b\fs24 Claim 7\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa120 The method of claim 1, wherein the authorization constraints include a maximum action sensitivity tier for the software agent.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa160\b\fs24 Claim 8\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa120 The method of claim 1, wherein intercepting the action request comprises intercepting at least one of an API call, a database query, a document retrieval, a network request, a payment operation, a code execution request, or a downstream agent invocation.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa160\b\fs24 Claim 9\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa120 The method of claim 1, further comprising computing a contextual risk value associated with the action request and dynamically narrowing the bounded permission set when the contextual risk value satisfies a threshold condition.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa160\b\fs24 Claim 10\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa120 The method of claim 9, wherein dynamically narrowing the bounded permission set comprises reducing an allowed tool set, reducing a resource scope, lowering an action sensitivity tier, suspending execution, or requiring additional approval.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa160\b\fs24 Claim 11\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa120 The method of claim 1, further comprising determining that the software agent requests delegation to a secondary software agent and, in response, generating a derivative authorization artifact for the secondary software agent, the derivative authorization artifact having a permission scope no broader than the scoped authorization artifact.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa160\b\fs24 Claim 12\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sa120\par
