\pard\sa160\b\fs24 Invention Theme\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa120 The invention concerns task-bound authorization of autonomous or semi-autonomous agents, with runtime enforcement and delegation containment. The core novelty emphasis is not merely authorizing an AI agent, but enforcing a bounded, machine-readable delegation scope during actual execution and across downstream agent chains.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa160\b\fs24 Likely Novelty Anchors\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\li720\fi-360 \bullet	ab compound authorization requiring principal authority, agent authority, and delegated authority\par
\pard\li720\fi-360 \bullet	ab short-lived delegation artifacts tied to a task, session, or conversation context\par
\pard\li720\fi-360 \bullet	ab gateway-mediated runtime enforcement for each agent action\par
\pard\li720\fi-360 \bullet	ab derivative child delegation with strict subset enforcement\par
\pard\li720\fi-360 \bullet	ab per-hierarchy classification caps and resource constraints\par
\pard\li720\fi-360 \bullet	ab delegation lineage through root and parent delegation identifiers\par
\pard\li720\fi-360 \bullet	ab dynamic narrowing and revocation during execution\par
\pard\li720\fi-360 \bullet	ab provenance linking approval, action, delegation, and output\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa160\b\fs24 Implementation Context\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\sa120 The current Stratium model includes:\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\li720\fi-360 \bullet	ab registered agents with trust tiers\par
\pard\li720\fi-360 \bullet	ab short-lived, platform-minted delegation tokens\par
\pard\li720\fi-360 \bullet	ab compound policy evaluation\par
\pard\li720\fi-360 \bullet	ab bounded action sensitivity tiers\par
\pard\li720\fi-360 \bullet	ab classification caps by hierarchy\par
\pard\li720\fi-360 \bullet	ab delegation chain depth limits\par
\pard\li720\fi-360 \bullet	ab gateway-mediated forwarding to protected services\par
\pard\li720\fi-360 \bullet	ab audit logging and chain lineage\par
